Trade Compliance, Logistics Operations, Customs
Brokers,

AEO ANNUAL SURVEILLANCE REVIEW -
Authorisation AEO-S-11284.
Your Authorized Economic Operator status
(Security and Safety, Tier S) enters its
annual surveillance review. The audit
team's on-site visit is planned for the
second week of next month; this notice
summarizes what to prepare.

1. AUTHORISATION & REVIEW SCOPE

  Authorisation:   AEO-S-11284
                   (Security & Safety,
                   valid to 2028-03)
  Holder:          Your company
                   (importer/exporter,
                   3 bonded facilities)
  Review type:     Annual surveillance
                   (desk + 2-day site
                   visit)
  Last review:     2026-02 - passed
                   with 3 observations
                   (all closed)
  Site visit:      Second week of next
                   month, facilities
                   FC-1 and FC-3
  Reference:       SR-2027-AEO-11284

2. RECORDS TO HAVE READY ON-SITE

  - Self-assessment questionnaire
    (2027 revision), all sections,
    changes since last review flagged
  - Business partner security file
    (vendor screening results,
    subcontracted transporters)
  - Security procedures pack: access
    control, seal management,
    incident response (incl. the
    October seal-discrepancy
    follow-up)
  - Training records: AWARE
    refresher completion

3. HOW SUBMISSION ACTUALLY WORKS

    1. Sign in to the customs
       trader gateway by typing
       the address yourself
       (the one used for your
       original AEO application
       and periodic declarations).
    2. The surveillance review task
       SR-2027-AEO-11284 appears
       under your authorisation;
       upload through that session
       only.
    3. Your broker may file on your
       behalf ONLY through their own
       registered gateway session
       with their own credentials.

  The Office of Customs will NEVER:
  - Email a documentation upload
    link "pre-linked to your
    review reference"
  - Operate "trader-compliance"
    or "customs-aeo-gov" style
    portal domains
  - Offer a broker lane that
    accepts multi-client files
    without per-client gateway
    authentication
  - Convert the pre-visit record
    check into an emailed
    "files not on record =
    authorisation gap" threat
    (incomplete files at visit
    time generate a written
    observation and a remediation
    window, not suspension)

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - The review schedule appears
    under your authorisation in
    the trader gateway
  - Programme terms (including
    the suspension and appeals
    framework) were issued with
    your authorisation letter;
    compare any threatened
    consequence against them

